// expect-error: cannot assign to '.len' of a slice
// BUG-967: the COMPOUND spelling of the same forge. `s.len += 100` is the same
// NODE_ASSIGN as `s.len = 100`, differing only in `assign.op` — so one test in the
// checker covers both, and this pins that it does. Written down because "two
// spellings of one operation" is a recurring shape here (see the CLAUDE.md table
// row: `x = pool.alloc()` vs `T x = pool.alloc()` lowered differently and every
// arm keyed on `dest_local` silently saw a temp).
u32 main() {
    u8[4] a;
    [*]u8 s = a;
    s.len += 100;
    s[50] = 1;
    return 0;
}
